  },
  {
    question: 'Have any spacecraft visited Uranus or Neptune?',
    answer: "Only one spacecraft has visited each of them: NASA's Voyager 2, which flew past Uranus in January 1986 and Neptune in August 1989. These remain the only close encounters with either planet. Voyager 2 discovered Uranus's 10 new moons, confirmed Neptune's Great Dark Spot, and found Triton's active geysers. As of 2026, no new missions have reached the ice giants, though NASA's Planetary Science Decadal Survey (2023–2032) ranked an Uranus orbiter and probe as the highest-priority large mission."
  }
